<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Brontë returns one week after starting doxylamine-pyridoxine, two tablets at bedtime, at 8 weeks 1 day. The bedtime dose helps her sleep, but nausea lasts most of the day and she now vomits four or five times a day. She keeps down small amounts of water, tea, and dry crackers most days and passes urine normally. She feels lightheaded only when she gets up quickly. She has stopped writing and lies down most of the afternoon. She has had no pain, bleeding, fever, or diarrhea. Her PUQE-24 score is 11 (moderate), up from 10. She weighs 44.0 kg, 4.3 percent below her pre-pregnancy weight. She saw Dr. Oyelaran-Hughes of maternal-fetal medicine this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Worse: vomiting four or five times a day</td></tr><tr><td>Intake</td><td>Small amounts of fluid and dry food kept down most days</td></tr><tr><td>Medication</td><td>Doxylamine-pyridoxine two tablets at bedtime; no daytime drowsiness</td></tr><tr><td>PUQE-24</td><td>11 (moderate), up from 10</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>44.0 kg, 4.3 percent below her pre-pregnancy weight</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

